analysis:
The only change in this file is a one-line signature update to the test-only stub WiringStubLanguageModel.prepare at line 158 of EngineV2ProductionWiringTests.swift. It now takes `state: LMOutput.State?, prefill: PrefillParameters` instead of `windowSize: Int?`, which tracks an upstream mlx-swift-lm LanguageModel protocol change. The stub still just returns `.tokens(input.text)`, and the file is under Tests/, so it ships in no production artifact. The supplied units are base-side text (lines 1221-2499) covering the unchanged surrounding tests, and they show no modification. Those tests cover:
- coordinator routing through the EngineV2 bridge;
- fail-closed tool_choice validation;
- rejection of forged schema metadata;
- cacheSalt plumbing (T-041: tenant scope passed as the cache salt);
- cancellation propagation (T-010);
- capacity heartbeats and KV-backend fallback reporting;
- prefill deadline configuration.

No security-relevant behavior changes. No trust boundary, authorization, attestation, encryption, cache storage or billing path is touched. The one open question for integration is the wider upstream API change (LMOutput.State and PrefillParameters). That change may alter production code outside this batch and should be reviewed in the files that actually use those types, such as the prefix-cache or prefill paths. It is not evidenced here.
